title: 'cumulus: add support for signed scheduling info'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |
    The slot-based collator gains the machinery for signing the scheduling info in a V3
    candidate's scheduling proof: the core selector, the claim queue offset, the approved
    peer id and the internal scheduling parent, signed with the Aura key that won the slot.
    The proof builder has two terminals: an unsigned one for initial submissions, which must
    stay valid without any additional signed data, with core selection taken from the
    block's UMP signals, and a signed one for resubmissions, where validators require the
    signature. The collator only produces initial submissions until resubmission support
    lands, so the signed terminal is exercised by tests only and nothing changes on the
    wire yet.
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-primitives-core
  bump: minor
- name: cumulus-pallet-parachain-system
  bump: none
